<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  What a development build is signed with. The App Sandbox is mandatory on the
  Mac App Store, and these two are the whole of what this application needs.

  `files.user-selected.read-write` is the grant a person gives by choosing a
  document in the open panel or a destination in the save panel. Nothing else
  is asked for: no network, no camera, no address book, and in particular no
  temporary exception. One path had to change to live inside this much, and
  it is recorded: `crates/segler-core/src/replace.rs` for the save, which
  cannot create a temporary file beside a document under this grant.

  The entitlement does nothing until it is inside a signature. An unsigned
  bundle carrying this file is not sandboxed, which is why the measurements in
  CHECKLIST.md are all made against a signed one, and why an Apple Development
  certificate is enough to make them. A Store build is signed with these two
  and the two identifiers the profile grants; the Store path of `build-app.sh` writes
  that file rather than this repository carrying the team identifier.

  Author: David M. Anderson
  Built with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
